  abstract = {Alzheimer’s disease (AD) is characterized by neocortical dissemination of neurofibrillary tangles (NFTs) while primary age‐related tauopathy (PART) has NFTs largely confined to the hippocampus and adjacent structures. Thus, PART and AD represent two extremes of a spectrum of NFT spread. We investigated epigenetic mechanisms of interindividual variation in NFT spread.},
