nd H. Sert and A. Stahl and T. Ziemons and H. Petersen and M. Martin and P. Asmuss and I. Babounikau and S. Baxter and O. Behnke and A. B. Martínez and A. Anuar and K. Borras and V. Botta and D. Brunner and A. Campbell and A. Cardini and P. Connor and S. Rodríguez and V. Danilov and A. Wit and M. Defranchis and L. Didukh and D. Damiani and G. Eckerlin and D. Eckstein and T. Eichhorn and A. Elwood and L. I. Banos and Ettore Gallo and A. Geiser and A. Giraldi and A. Grohsjean and M. Guthoff and M. Haranko and A. Harb and A. Jafari and N. Z. Jomhari and Hannes Jung and A. Kasem and M. Kasemann and H. Kaveh and J. Keaveney and C. Kleinwort and J. Knolle and D. Krücker and W. Lange and T. Lenz and J. Lidrych and K. Lipka and W. Lohmann and R. Mankel and I. Melzer-Pellmann and J. Metwally and A. Meyer and M. Meyer and M. Missiroli and J. Mnich and A. Mussgiller and V. Myronenko and Y. Otarid and D. P. Adán and S. Pflitsch and D. Pitzl and A. Raspereza and A. Saggio and A. Saibel and M. Savitskyi and V. Scheurer and P. Schütze and C. Schwanenberger and R. Shevchenko and A. Singh and R. Ricardo and H. Tholen and N. Tonon and O. Turkot and A. Vagnerini and M. Klundert and R. Walsh and D. Walter and Y. Wen and K. Wichmann and C. Wissing and S. Wuchterl and O. Zenaiev and R. Žlebčík and R. Aggleton and S. Bein and L. Benato and A. Benecke and K. Leo and T. Dreyer and A. Ebrahimi and F. Feindt and A. Fröhlich and C. Garbers and E. Garutti and D. Gonzalez and P. Gunnellini and J. Haller and A. Hinzmann and A. Karavdina},
  year = {2020},
  abstract = {Abstract Measurements of production cross sections of W Z and same-sign W W boson pairs in association with two jets in proton-proton collisions at s = 13 TeV at the LHC are reported. The data sample corresponds to an integrated luminosity of 137 fb − 1 , collected with the CMS detector during 2016–2018. The measurements are performed in the leptonic decay modes and , where l , l ′ = e , . Differential fiducial cross sections as functions of the invariant masses of the jet and charged lepton pairs, as well as of the leading-lepton transverse momentum, are measured for W ± W ± production and are consistent with the standard model predictions. The dependence of differential cross sections on the invariant mass of the jet pair is also measured for W Z production. An observation of electroweak production of W Z boson pairs is reported with an observed (expected) significance of 6.8 (5.3) standard deviations. Constraints are obtained on the structure of quartic vector boson interactions in the framework of effective field theory.},
