  abstract = {Drug‐resistant epilepsy patients show worse outcomes after resection when standard neuroimaging is nonlesional, which occurs in one‐third of patients. In prior work, we employed 2‐D glutamate imaging, Glutamate Chemical Exchange Saturation Transfer (GluCEST), to lateralize seizure onset in nonlesional temporal lobe epilepsy (TLE) based on increased ipsilateral GluCEST signal in the total hippocampus and hippocampal head. We present a significant advancement to single‐slice GluCEST imaging, allowing for three‐dimensional analysis of brain glutamate networks.},
