einer and K. Martin‐Cook and Michael D. Devous and A. Levey and J. Lah and J. Cellar and Jeffrey M. Burns and H. Anderson and R. Swerdlow and L. Apostolova and K. Tingus and Ellen Woo and Daniel H. Silverman and Po H. Lu and G. Bartzokis and N. Graff-Radford and F. Parfitt and Tracy Kendall and Heather K. Johnson and M. Farlow and A. Hake and Brandy R. Matthews and S. Herring and Cynthia Hunt and Christopher H. van Dyck and Richard E. Carson and M. Macavoy and H. Chertkow and H. Bergman and C. Hosein and B. Stefanovic and Curtis Caldwell and G. Hsiung and Howard H. Feldman and B. Mudge and M. Assaly and Andrew Kertesz and J. Rogers and Charles Bernick and D. Munic and D. Kerwin and M. Mesulam and K. Lipowski and Chuang-Kuo Wu and N. Johnson and C. Sadowsky and Walter Martínez and Teresa Villena and R. Turner and K. Johnson and Brigid Reynolds and R. Sperling and K. Johnson and G. Marshall and Meghan T. Frey and B. Lane and A. Rosen and Jared S. Tinklenberg and Marwan N. Sabbagh and C. Belden and S. Jacobson and Sherye A. Sirrel and N. Kowall and Ronald J. Killiany and Andrew E. Budson and Alexander Norbash and P. L. Johnson and Joanne S. Allard and Alan J. Lerner and P. Ogrocki and Leon Hudson and Evan F. Fletcher and O. Carmichael and J. Olichney and C. DeCarli and S. Kittur and Michael Borrie and T. Lee and R. Bartha and Sterling C. Johnson and Sanjay Asthana and C. Carlsson and S. Potkin and Adrian Preda and D. Nguyen and P. Tariot and Stephanie A. Reeder and V. Bates and H. Capote and M. Rainka and D. Scharre and M. Kataki and Anahita Adeli and E. Zimmerman and D. Celmins and Alice D. Brown and Godfrey D. Pearlson and K. Blank and K. Anderson and R. Santulli and T. Kitzmiller and E. Schwartz and K. Sink and Jeffrey D. Williamson and P. Garg and F. Watkins and Brian R. Ott and H. Querfurth and G. Tremont and S. Salloway and Paul F. Malloy and S. Correia and Howard J. Rosen and B. Miller and Jacobo E. Mintzer and K. Spicer and David Bachman and S. Pasternak and I. Rachinsky and D. Drost and Nunzio Pomara and R. Hernando and A. Sarrael and Susan K. Schultz and L. Ponto and H. Shim and K. Smith and Norman R. Relkin and G. Chaing and Lisa Raudin and Amanda G. Smith and K. Fargher and B. A. Raj and T. Neylan and J. Grafman and M. Davis and Rosemary H. Morrison and J. Hayes and Shannon Finley and K. Friedl and Debra A. Fleischman and K. Arfanakis and O. James and D. Massoglia and J. Fruehling and S. Harding and E. Peskind and E. Petrie and Gail Li and J. Yesavage and Joy Taylor and A. Furst},
  year = {2017},
  abstract = {The heterogeneity of neurodegenerative diseases is a key confound to disease understanding and treatment development, as study cohorts typically include multiple phenotypes on distinct disease trajectories. Here we introduce a machine-learning technique—Subtype and Stage Inference (SuStaIn)—able to uncover data-driven disease phenotypes with distinct temporal progression patterns, from widely available cross-sectional patient studies. Results from imaging studies in two neurodegenerative diseases reveal subgroups and their distinct trajectories of regional neurodegeneration. In genetic frontotemporal dementia, SuStaIn identifies genotypes from imaging alone, validating its ability to identify subtypes; further the technique reveals within-genotype heterogeneity. In Alzheimer’s disease, SuStaIn uncovers three subtypes, uniquely characterising their temporal complexity. SuStaIn provides fine-grained patient stratification, which substantially enhances the ability to predict conversion between diagnostic categories over standard models that ignore subtype (p = 7.18 × 10−4) or temporal stage (p = 3.96 × 10−5). SuStaIn offers new promise for enabling disease subtype discovery and precision medicine. Progressive diseases tend to be heterogeneous in their underlying aetiology mechanism, disease manifestation, and disease time course. Here, Young and colleagues devise a computational method to account for both phenotypic heterogeneity and temporal heterogeneity, and demonstrate it using two neurodegenerative disease cohorts.},
  doi = {10.1038/s41467-018-05892-0},
  pmid = {30323170},
  month = {12},
  journal = {Nature Communications},
  volume = {9},
  altmetric = {true},
  dimensions = {true},
  note = {Cited by 95},
  pdf = {https://www.nature.com/articles/s41467-018-05892-0.pdf},
}

